# Pinned SQLite runtime for the server image (deploy/compose/Dockerfile.server, stage "sqlite"). The
# same values are the ARG defaults in the Dockerfile and the build args in docker-compose.yml, so a plain
# `docker build` / `docker compose build` is PINNED BY DEFAULT; this file is the human-readable record
# and what CI loads. Provenance (verified by the operator on 2026-09-13T17:34:15Z): the official HTTPS
# amalgamation ZIP fetched with certificate validation, ZIP CRCs checked, sqlite3.c SHA3-256 and the
# C/header version + source id matched against https://www.sqlite.org/releaselog/3_51_3.html. The
# ARCHIVE digests below are computed from those verified ZIP bytes (the official page publishes the
# sqlite3.c digest, not an archive digest); the build verifies archive SHA3-256, archive SHA-256 AND
# the official sqlite3.c SHA3-256 before compiling, and the image attests the exact sqlite_source_id().
# 3.51.3 carries the WAL-reset fix (3.44.6 and 3.50.7 are the named backports).
SQLITE_VERSION=3.51.3
SQLITE_ARCHIVE_URL=https://www.sqlite.org/2026/sqlite-amalgamation-3510300.zip
SQLITE_ARCHIVE_BYTES=2876305
SQLITE_ARCHIVE_SHA3_256=ced02ff9738970f338c9c8e269897b554bcda73f6cf1029d49459e1324dbeaea
SQLITE_ARCHIVE_SHA256=acb1e6f5d832484bf6d32b681e858c38add8b2acdfd42ac5df24b8afb46552b4
SQLITE_SQLITE3_C_SHA3_256=32d5424f97e0a7fc5ed2f6335afbb58be4e0298bd7117a34e39d345ff13d859e
SQLITE_SOURCE_ID="2026-03-13 10:38:09 737ae4a34738ffa0c3ff7f9bb18df914dd1cad163f28fd6b6e114a344fe6d618"
